Input: {"question": "What is the format of KSGF?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 0, "end": 90, "text": "KSGF-FM KSGF-FM (104.1 FM) is a radio station broadcasting a News Talk Information format."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 91, "end": 180, "text": "Licensed to Ash Grove, Missouri, United States, it serves the Springfield, Missouri area."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 181, "end": 217, "text": "The station is owned by SummitMedia."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 218, "end": 251, "text": "Journal Communications and the E."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 252, "end": 254, "text": "W."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 255, "end": 381, "text": "Scripps Company announced on July 30, 2014 that the two companies would merge to create a new broadcast company under the E.W."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 382, "end": 473, "text": "Scripps Company name that owned the two companies' broadcast properties, including KSGF-FM."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 474, "end": 558, "text": "The transaction was completed in 2015, pending shareholder and regulatory approvals."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "start": 559, "end": 663, "text": "Scripps exited radio in 2018; the Springfield stations went to SummitMedia in a four-market, $47 million"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d01", "start": 0, "end": 659, "text": "hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shorte