c_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d03", "start": 309, "end": 457, "text": "Weekday programming includes a local morning show called, \"KSGF Mornings with Nick Reed,\" hosted by Nick Reed with executive producer Kortni Tucker."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d03", "start": 458, "end": 617, "text": "The remainder of the weekday is taken up by syndicated shows hosted by Glenn Beck, Dana Loesch, Sean Hannity, Mark Levin, Michael Savage, the Red Eye Radio and"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d04", "start": 0, "end": 4, "text": "Inc."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d04", "start": 5, "end": 68, "text": ", reached an agreement to sell the station to Springcom , Inc ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d04", "start": 69, "end": 167, "text": "The deal was approved by the FCC on February 25 , and the transaction was consummated on March 8 ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d04", "start": 168, "end": 264, "text": "[ 19 ] In January 1985 , KGBX began broadcasting in AM stereo using the Motorola C-QUAM system ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d04", "start": 265, "end": 307, "text": "[ 20 ] In February 1986 , Springcom , Inc."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d04", "start": 308, "end": 371, "text": ", contracted to sell the station to KGBX Communications , Inc ."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d04", "start": 372, "end": 481, "text": "The deal was approved by the FCC on March 18 , 1986 , and the transaction was consummated on April 7 , 1986 ."}, "D5S8": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d04", "start": 482, "end": 483, "text": "["}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0251-f9dac6bf0467:d00:c0", "entity": "KSGF"